{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Agent Operations: submit one payout or fee configuration as originally agreed (destination, network, asset, fee rate, fixed fee, caps and scope) with its approval record and the agreement\u2019s change rules, a proposed change and any consent record for it. The signed report says whether the change can take effect under the original agreement, needs the counterparty\u2019s fresh approval first (naming what changed: new destination or payout route, higher fee, wider scope) or is outside the agreement entirely, change by change. Configuration-change governance: payout readiness for a single payment is wever_payout-readiness-check. Verdict outside_agreement, counterparty_approval_required or can_take_effect. POST /api/payout-change-check. Reads only the material in the call: no network request, fetch, money movement, message, sharing, configuration change or external write. Paid URL: 0.10 USDC per call on Base via x402 exact, with the shared 10 signed-wallet free calls per rolling 30 days. Bind X-Wever-Wallet-Proof to the exact JSON arguments and the tool route. Returns a report with an Ed25519 signed receipt. Contract: /api/agent-operations-contract. Human page: https://weverlabs.com/agent-operations/.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"agreement":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The agreement\u2019s rule for each kind of change (destination_change for a new destination, network or asset; fee_increase; scope_change; other_change): allowed, notice, counterparty_approval or not_allowed.","properties":{"destination_change":{"enum":["allowed","notice","counterparty_approval","not_allowed"]},"fee_increase":{"enum":["allowed","notice","counterparty_approval","not_allowed"]},"max_fee_rate":{"anyOf":[{"maximum":100,"minimum":0,"type":"number"},{"maxLength":20,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}],"description":